# Asset Storage And Delivery

- Store large creator media in first-party object storage, not in Postgres rows or device-local paths.
- Use relational tables for canonical asset metadata, ownership, checksums, and delivery references.
- Treat offline device files as caches only, never as publishable asset identifiers.
- Generate standard derivatives for cards, details, and reading surfaces instead of serving originals everywhere.
- Keep unpublished or review-stage assets private until they are explicitly approved for public delivery.
- Prefer stable canonical object paths over free-form third-party URLs for first-party creator content.
